	)
	(text "Data straight from the Pico's USB test points TP3 (D+) / TP2 (D-) (U1, sheet 1), behind the 27R\nseries resistors on the Pico module. The Pico must be soldered FLAT on the board (castellated edge or\nthrough-hole pins, no header) so TP1-TP3 can be soldered from the back of the card.\nWith the Pico on headers or in a socket the TP pads do not reach the card: wire TP1-TP3 to the holes,\nor use a micro-USB OTG adapter on the Pico (with jumper J7) as on v1.3.0. Never use both at once.\nVBUS from ISA +5V via F1 (resettable, 0.5 A hold), C34 bulk. The Pico VBUS pin is not used for this port.\nU12 (ESD array, SOT-23-6) is optional."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 63.5 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cee73a33-f64d-58ec-a6fd-493d16870eec")
	)
